ny message that I was  getting a reward for self play thurs but  it seems like super hot has a lot of  directions it could grow in if they just  kind of refine these mechanics and tone  down the visual effects on the  storytelling yeah I think there's a  great foundation there and the gameplay  can see of time not moving until you do  is really cool and I like that you  brought up the stealth because I was  I've been playing a few other stealth  games right now and it would be cool the  fact that time is moving so slowly I  think would make it a lot more tense if  you're moving in slow motion or at least  advancing time between slow motion and  you're just worried like oh [ __ ] is he  gonna see me right now or not am I going  to be able to avoid a gunfight but I  kind of agree with you right now as far  as that overarching storyline goes I  feel like it's just them trying to force  something on me because the game is so  bare-boned right now as it is I think  I'd rather definitely see them build it  in a gameplay direction first and  foremost and if they happen to tack on  like some sort of overarching narrative  that makes me question what I've been  doing that's really cool it's a bonus  but that's not what I'm looking for in a  game like that so right now I'm kind of  just expecting them to like you said  expand different directions gameplay  wise awesome thanks Mike thanks Aaron
 

